"File > New Database" on wasm triggers a browser save-file dialog that
downloads an empty file and hands DB Browser a filename it can't
actually write back to, leaving the app in a "no database file opened"
state. DB Browser already has a fileNewInMemoryDatabase() action that
works correctly here — reroute fileNew() to it on wasm so both menu
entries behave the same and the user can't fall into the broken path.

--- a/src/MainWindow.cpp
+++ b/src/MainWindow.cpp
@@ -600,6 +600,13 @@ void MainWindow::activateFields(bool enable)

 void MainWindow::fileNew()
 {
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    // Reroute to in-memory: the desktop "pick a filename, sqlite3 creates it"
+    // flow doesn't work in the browser because save-file-picker returns a
+    // one-shot download handle, not a writable filesystem path.
+    fileNewInMemoryDatabase(/* open_create_dialog */ true);
+    return;
+#endif
     QString fileName = FileDialog::getSaveFileName(
                            CreateDatabaseFile,
                            this,
